``` Every result file carries `"token_source": "engine"`. If it ever says `chars/4`, the number next to it is not to be trusted. ### It streams, so the first token can be timed separately Time to first token and tokens per second measure different things — reading the prompt and writing the answer. A non-streaming request collapses them into one number and loses both. ```python
